# Fingerprints gitleaks should not report, one per line, in the form
#   <commit>:<path>:<rule-id>:<line>
#
# Prefer a scoped rule allowlist in `.gitleaks.toml` over an entry here. A
# fingerprint is pinned to one commit, so it silently stops applying the moment
# history is rewritten, and it records no reason. The allowlist in the config
# forgives a documented *shape* instead, and survives a rebase.
#
# Adding an entry here hides a finding, so it is never a unilateral call: a new
# suppression needs Indy's explicit approval, and the default is to restructure
# so the scanner passes unassisted. Removing one needs no approval.
#
# Empty as of Aug 17, 2026. Two entries inherited from indykish/dotfiles pinned
# commit df44ade3, which does not exist in this repository, so they suppressed
# nothing. The `.oracle/ruleset.lock` digests that replaced them now live in
# `.gitleaks.toml` as a path-and-line-scoped allowlist on `generic-api-key`.
